================================================================================
## Compute the mapped triples once and reset `_inferred` in the main build
================================================================================

Context: Task 0 of incremental triple materialization. A build evaluated the
R2RML gateway VIEW three times: once for the `…_data` CTAS, once for the
COUNT(*) and once for the stream into the graph store. The Databricks backend also never reset
`…_inferred` in the main build, so reasoning or cohort triples written for the
previous data were served next to the rebuilt data; only the standalone
Databricks build pipeline truncated it. Once `…_data` is a materialized table
the count and the stream now read it instead of the VIEW (Lakeflow keeps syncing
the VIEW, see the fix section below), and the main build empties `…_inferred` (a failure fails the build). A
pass-through `view` `…_data` costs the same as the VIEW, so the VIEW stays the
source in that mode. The new logic lives in a collaborator class so
`_BuildPipeline` stays inside its architecture-ratchet size budget.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py (new)
   Collaborator with static methods: `triples_source_relation` (the `…_data`
   table when materialized as a table, else the VIEW), `reset_inferred_companion`
   (Databricks backend only: ensure `…_inferred`, strict TRUNCATE, refresh the
   `…_graph` union view; `tm.fail_task` and `False` on error, debug log and skip
   for Lakebase/Neo4j), `trace_fields` (`triples_source`, `inferred_reset`) and
   `persist_last_build_to_registry` (moved out of the pipeline, unchanged).
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/__init__.py
   Re-export `TwinBuildPostMaterialize`.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   Thin hooks: `_triples_source_relation`, `_count_source_triples` (with
   `_count_view_triples` kept as an alias), `_reset_inferred_companion` called in
   `run()` after `_materialize_data_table` and before the apply step. The full
   rebuild count and stream read `_triples_source_relation()`. `_materialize_data_table` records
   `data_relation_mode` and asks for `object_hash` only for a table that Lakeflow
   will sync once the sync source moves off the VIEW. `_record_build_run` merges `triples_source` and `inferred_reset`
   into the build-run entry. `_persist_last_build_to_registry` is a one-line
   delegate (Extract Class, `_BuildPipeline` 1452 -> 1411 LOC).
4. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py
   `build_ctas_sql`, `materialize_from_view` and `apply_data_relation` take
   `with_object_hash` (default False, so every other caller is unchanged). When
   True the CTAS also copies `object_hash`, which the Lakeflow synced-table
   primary key needs and which `_data` did not have before.
5. tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_compute_once.py (new)
   Table mode reads `…_data` for count and stream and evaluates the VIEW exactly
   once; view mode keeps the VIEW; synced CTAS carries `object_hash`; Databricks reset order and failure
   handling; other backends untouched; trace keys.
6. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_package.py
   Both shapes of the CTAS SQL and `apply_data_relation` forwarding.
7. tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_materialize.py
   Four existing test doubles accept the new keyword (`**_`).

